86556331} :answer-field/id #uuid "b816efcf-ee31-5d4d-b5a0-f4d15dfc9f02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556332}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e3cd9a6-4a6e-5025-b51b-7ed39764e4aa" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=17$ for $x\\le 0,$ between the surfaces $z=x$ and $z={y}^{2}.$ Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/24/249116dd79140b8e49d64902c46a3f0bc7c6411c9f8e7129faf38c64e7cc859e.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-half of a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{17}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z={y}^{2}={r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{17},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta <\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\,r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le z\\le {r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}-(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}r({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46301c75-2fec-592f-826f-de2f2329166d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{81 - r^{2}}}r^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556302} {:answer/id #uuid "4d147f3c-7c7a-55fd-8060-25977335911c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{81 - r}}r^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556303} {:answer/id #uuid "687972b9-0c2c-5709-9a7a-2752f5b7a00d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{81 - r^{2}}}r\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556310} {:answer/id #uuid "977e3699-4ca1-57bc-b535-c8ccdef87b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{81 - r^{2}}}r\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556322} {:answer/id #uuid "f1111443-077e-5195-879d-f02a7a1b30e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{81 - r}}r\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "687972b9-0c2c-5709-9a7a-2752f5b7a00d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{81 - r^{2}}}r\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556310} :answer-field/id #uuid "c47faa4e-16be-5d4f-af17-692c137897af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556338}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62da815e-5934-5e3e-9bc6-bd904287e19a" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ for $x\\le 0$ and $y\\ge 0,$ between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z=\\sqrt{81-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}.$ Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/3e/3e51a479b8fe2a00f7b51a8613fe2cb6a45d790d737637c31b7858766e0491ff.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-quarter of a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=\\sqrt{81-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}=\\sqrt{81-{r}^{2}}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{81-{r}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{81-{r}^{2}}}r\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a89ee8e-7e15-5633-8d7b-1924dc4d1c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556291} {:answer/id #uuid "6eac9f5e-670c-54d8-810c-719b5a5dbc81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556312} {:answer/id #uuid "9c71522c-2eb4-5a48-9b3e-85cfdbf7c81f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8}r^{4} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556324} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c33169-a9bf-56cb-b9c3-638a7bc5f3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{24}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556326} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4de96a-0e7c-5667-9175-3198f42cd7dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{24}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556344}] :answer-field/co