e r\\le 2 \\sqrt{6},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\pi,r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\le z\\le r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V&=\\iiint_\\Delta z((r\\cos\\theta)^2-(r\\sin\\theta)^2)\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta rz(r^2\\cos^2\\theta-r^2\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z\\cos(2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0630c64a-1afb-51f8-84e7-89391db92821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{r}^{4}r\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556288} {:answer/id #uuid "2735da5a-71b8-5e58-beb0-ff742aae5ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{r^{2}}^{4}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556294} {:answer/id #uuid "40378672-56df-5c9f-9860-e8215b6cd36d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r}^{4}r^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556299} {:answer/id #uuid "4efc9014-7ea1-5a48-a360-c10927768451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r}^{4}r\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556305} {:answer/id #uuid "e186b187-c630-5380-9507-073f03e8db07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r^{2}}^{4}r^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40378672-56df-5c9f-9860-e8215b6cd36d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r}^{4}r^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556299} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4c768b6-182e-56f5-b00b-887eff258f6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556330}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2ff09b0-b6eb-591a-8929-4799745e83bf" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ between the surfaces $z=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and $z=4.$ Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/f8/f869ef32fb741040d355c3280da541178bcac9b52477ebfa7d078d8b832a5903.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=r,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=4.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\\,r\\le z\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}r\\sqrt{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r}^{4}{r}^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ef1460b-69ae-51db-9b0f-38d59059ba70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{17}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556297} {:answer/id #uuid "5e4f373a-a4f0-5a51-a093-838770927ab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556307} {:answer/id #uuid "64deca10-88b4-5e7a-b5e9-5a0dc46c6381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556309} {:answer/id #uuid "727d0f0f-e7a5-5179-b828-68cc0999f3fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{4} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556314} {:answer/id #uuid "7f900858-3ef0-5041-8288-ecff79ae4ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{17}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e4f373a-a4f0-5a51-a093-838770927ab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556307} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8859d70-7ca1-534f-afa2-e0f12da33a5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556341}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe023327-0703-5ca3-ba96-2cf3d63544fc" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=17$ for $x\\le 0$ and $y\\ge 0$, between the surfaces $z=x$ and $z=y^{2} + 12$. Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates.\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/0e/0e609e4abfb4512377285af757fa4002f8e976352c72e54a808d156a781298b1.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-quarter of a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{17}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=x=r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=y^{2} + 12=r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{17},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\pi,r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\le z\\le r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V&=\\iiint_\\Delta z((r\\cos\\theta)^2-(r\\sin\\theta)^2)\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta rz(r^2\\cos^2\\theta-r^2\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z\\cos(2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565440 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1210b916-b4ea-5cba-9d0b-88ffd8db5b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{r}^{2}+9}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+1}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564968} {:answer/id #uuid "609ff4b7-e3e7-59dc-bd1a-628643aa1eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{r+9}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+1}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565086} {:answer/id #uuid "8405bbf3-f8ff-5256-911f-3b037174a5a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{r+9}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+1}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565143} {:answer/id #uuid "b198dc59-a572-58ee-95d9-e619f5217eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{r}^{2}+9}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+1}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565202} {:answer/id #uuid "b3bf8739-96ec-51ef-aae4-6adf4a13a184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{r}^{2}+9}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+1}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1210b916-b4ea-5cba-9d0b-88ffd8db5b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{r}^{2}+9}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+1}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564968} :answer-field/id #uuid "b54ca112-ae75-5f34-8db6-6d52d5ea414f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565376}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6699d568-4112-5bd7-abf4-a27c0cbde6ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-161614" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ for $y\\le 0,$ between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+9.$ Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/35/350b2dc98a09957c17f1ab629e21021c30fcccd9443068c722fe7565f04dcbfe.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-half of a right vertical cylinder of radius $2$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+9={r}^{2}+9.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le {r}^{2}+9\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{\\mathrm{Δ}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}\\theta )^{2}+1}}\\cdot r\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathrm{d}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}r\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{\\mathrm{Δ}}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta +{r}^{2}{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta +1}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathrm{d}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}r\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{\\mathrm{Δ}}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}({\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta +{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta )+1}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathrm{d}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}r\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{{\\color{blue}\\pi }}}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{{\\color{blue}{r}^{2}+9}}}\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{{\\color{blue}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+1}}}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathrm{d}z\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}r\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Cylindrical Solid"}]}
